DUMP slot FILE
  That slot's program saved whole and where it is: its 64K (the program,
  its stack and registers, its screen) and its state. A running one is paused
  for it and goes on after. Refused for a slot with a file open, a claim, a
  port or a socket (they can't go with it).
REVIVE slot FILE
  The file back into that slot (closed, or at its command line), paused:
  UNPAUSE slot and it goes on from where it was. Another slot is fine; a dump
  from another build of CyborgOS isn't taken. Its scrollback and store are new.
